Z||000000||Homicidal||09-15-2000||05:41 PM||||I saw a fellow Fiero driver, some oriental guy.  Had the most UGLY Fiero I have EVER seen.<P>Green with sections (sail panels and trunk + spolier) painted ugly white.  Horrible!<P>Plus, TWO (not one, but TWO) Spoilers!! One spoiler was really nice, direct off an Mr2. Looked REALLY good.<P>The other was a horribly high "ricer" spoiler, which absolutely killed the look of the car (more than the crap paint job)!<P>But anyways, has anybody ever attempted to put an Mr2 spolier on a Fiero?  I might try this at my local boneyard!||||reg||10
Z||000001||Songman||09-15-2000||06:57 PM||||I'll tell you a spoiler that looks great on a Fiero... the big trunk spoiler like on a Saleen Mustang! My buddy is redoing one in his paint shop. The white spoiler was lying there one day so I took it over and sat it on the back of the white 88 coupe. It fit perfectly! Well.. almost,At the very back it hangs over each side of the trunk about 1/8". I can live with that...<P>It really made the car look sporty! I already have the 5 spoke alloy wheels and 225/50R15s so it looked natural. The only problem is with trying to see over the dang thing in the rearview mirror! The things we put up with to look good!||||reg||3
Z||000002||Homicidal||09-15-2000||07:04 PM||||See, the Mr2 spoiler I saw looked perfect, better than the stock Fiero one!||||reg||1
Z||000003||TwisT||09-15-2000||08:12 PM||||...Funny we mention the Saleen wing...  will be installing the wing this winter during a complete tear-down of my '88 GT.  One of the best looking wings,  looks wicked but still not tacky like so many of the ricer-wings.<P>I'll be sure to post pics on my website showing her progress.  =)||||reg||1
